{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unusual-carneous-alleycat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Why\nEpic polite-antivirus-bedbug (`536b-8930-b922-4063`) has an acceptance box that reads: \"docs/concurrency.md §I1 moved 'implemented'; residual pack size quantified; W3 set; W1/W2 filed\". On origin/main 9d10232dd89, the `.retired` lifecycle paragraph in docs/concurrency.md §I1 still says the history reclamation is \"specified by ADR 0106\" and tracked under the epic. The reclamation is now built and was run against production `tickets` on 2026-11-20 18:14 PST, so the doc is out of date.\n\n## What changes\nOne paragraph in `docs/concurrency.md` §I1 (\"`.retired` lifecycle\"). No code, config key, env var, flag or test changes.\n\nThe rewritten paragraph will state:\n1. Retired files stay in the working tree. The branch-wide `.retired` sweep was not built: story mystical-capsizable-ibis closed wontfix, because the files are blobs and the guarded pack is blobless.\n2. Remote-anchored below-horizon commit/tree history reclamation (ADR 0106) is **implemented**. It names the modules: `rebar._store.reclaim_eligibility` (horizon eligibility), `rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse` (core-git collapse plus ledger re-resolution and `enforce_since` re-anchor), `rebar._commands.reclaim_publish` (lease-guarded publish-swap, S3 bundle-set replacement, rollback), `rebar._commands.reclaim_dry_run` (shadow-clone dry-run harness) and `rebar._store.stale_override` (reconnect override). It points to the existing §I5 reconnect and publish paragraphs.\n3. Reclamation **was run** on 2026-11-20 18:14 PST: `tickets` efcf5ae2b97 -> 6a6dda16fc7 under a lease-guarded atomic push, with backup ref `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261121T021044Z` at the old tip. Commits went from 312,156 to 14,235. The blobless pack measured on the proof's fake remote went from 625 MiB to 108 MiB.\n4. The measured residual: a fresh blobless bare clone of origin `tickets` at 4fd8b099490 (14,375 commits), taken 2026-11-20 21:13 PST, has `size-pack` 122,794 KiB (about 120 MiB). The paragraph also says the residual grows with write volume until the next reclaim. The `verify-identity.yml` pack budget now measures only the code checkout (cc4a23a2405, bc25-1351), so the budget no longer gates this residual. The old claim that \"the pack the CI budget guards is blobless tickets history\" is corrected to match.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `.retired` lifecycle paragraph in `docs/concurrency.md` §I1 says the ADR 0106 history reclamation is implemented and names the five modules listed above. `grep -n \"implemented\" docs/concurrency.md` shows the line inside §I1.\n- [ ] The paragraph records that the reclaim was run: date, old and new tip, backup ref, and commit counts before and after.\n- [ ] The paragraph records the measured residual blobless pack size with its date and commit count: 122,794 KiB at 4fd8b099490.\n- [ ] The paragraph no longer says the reclamation is only \"specified\" and no longer says the CI budget guards tickets history.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, or each failure is shown to be environmental. The Gerrit change gets `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` and merges to main.\n\n## File impact\n- `docs/concurrency.md` — §I1 `.retired` lifecycle paragraph only.\n\n## Portability\nDocumentation only. Nothing depends on a CI provider.\n\n## Testing\nThis is a documentation-only change, so no new test is needed. The docs-drift and doc-policy tests in `make verify` cover it.","id":"596a-8b1b-299e-49e1","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Mark ADR 0106 history reclamation implemented in concurrency.md I1"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795238106372982001,"uuid":"7176c52c-2b68-4a66-8992-edd52626e6fc"}